Command:	FIND <string>
Purpose:	Locate files which contain <string> in their titles
Available at:	All command prompts

The FIND command has been provided so that you may quickly locate any file that you have access to on the system.  A file will be found if its name contains the <string> that you specify.

CNet will use the familiar "Browse" routines to display files.  This allows you to readily download, select, examine, or grab found files.
